					<description><![CDATA[<p>The D.C. Circuit Court of Appeals has ruled against the Trump administration's order to keep the J.H. Campbell coal-fired power plant in Michigan operating. The decision that could impact other orders that have been issued to keep U.S. coal-fired power plants operating past their scheduled retirement dates.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.powermag.com/court-rules-against-trump-order-to-keep-michigan-coal-fired-plant-operating/">Court Rules Against Trump Order to Keep Michigan Coal-Fired Plant Operating</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.powermag.com">POWER Magazine</a>.</p>
<p><img width="350" height="267" src="https://www.powermag.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/jh-campbell-complex-waterway-descriptor3.png" class="attachment-post-thumbnail size-post-thumbnail wp-post-image" alt="jh-campbell-complex-waterway-descriptor3" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" srcset="https://www.powermag.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/jh-campbell-complex-waterway-descriptor3.png 350w, https://www.powermag.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/jh-campbell-complex-waterway-descriptor3-300x229.png 300w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" /></p>]]></description>
		
